# Cache busting

Local CSS, JS, images, and favicons are loaded with a `?v=` query in `index.html`. Browsers cache those files; a new `v` is what makes visitors see the change.

## When to bump

If you edit or replace any file that `index.html` loads from this repo, set that URL's `?v=` to a new value. Use `YYYYMMDD` (add `a`, `b`, … if the same day already shipped).

Only bump the assets that actually changed. Do not bump on copy-only HTML edits. Do not add `?v=` to external URLs (e.g. rulergame.net).

## Example

```html
<!-- CSS file changed today -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/css/rulerpie.css?v=20260819">

<!-- JS unchanged — leave it -->
<script src="assets/script/rulerpie.js?v=20260818" defer></script>
```

New local assets must include `?v=` when added to `index.html`.
